    <briefdescription>
<para>Comparator on <computeroutput><ref refid="structgb_a_1_1spair" kindref="compound">gbA::spair</ref>*</computeroutput> used by the default Groebner basis driver to order its S-pair queue. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Orders descending by sugar <computeroutput>deg</computeroutput> (largest first <mdash/> the queue processes pairs of equal degree as a cohort), then by <computeroutput><ref refid="structspair" kindref="compound">spair</ref></computeroutput> type, then by lead term of the S-polynomial. The two helpers <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_poly_sorter_a60d77d891d2c8f931b13b2343506d6e3_1a60d77d891d2c8f931b13b2343506d6e3" kindref="member">compare</ref></computeroutput> (returning <computeroutput><ref refid="submodules_2mathicgb_2src_2mathicgb_2polyring_8hpp_aaf56b99cbe34023f42ce5b7878c827d8_1aaf56b99cbe34023f42ce5b7878c827d8" kindref="member">LT</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="submodules_2mathicgb_2src_2mathicgb_2polyring_8hpp_abaab8d42f075ee8ddc9b70951d3fd6cd_1abaab8d42f075ee8ddc9b70951d3fd6cd" kindref="member">EQ</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="submodules_2mathicgb_2src_2mathicgb_2polyring_8hpp_ab89310b3f2f97e4e9415fc5a51549612_1ab89310b3f2f97e4e9415fc5a51549612" kindref="member">GT</ref></computeroutput>) and the standard <computeroutput>operator()</computeroutput>-style entry are both supplied so the same functor can drive both manual sorting and <computeroutput>std::priority_queue</computeroutput>-style containers. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
